Slight tangent here, but that brings to mind something I've thought odd 
about wishing for some time. Most objects can be wished for by giving 
only the part after "of". For example Force Bolt will give you the 
spellbook, Death will give you the wand, Gain Level will give you the 
potion, and so on. But for some reason... Not so with amulets. A wish 
for "Life Saving" for example will not be recognized. The same is true 
of magical armor (eg. "Brilliance" don't work), but armor isn't named as 
systematically so I wouldn't really expect it to work.

Of course you have to be careful with this kind of wish because more 
than one object type may have that decription (eg, polymorph =+/ or Fire 
?/). But on the other hand you're partlly protected from typos and 
spelling errors this way. Wish for a "Ring of Fire Resistence" (with an 
e) and you get a random ring. If you just wish for "Fire Resistence" it 
will tell you it doesn't exist and give you another chance.

